<section>

<div class="lesson">

<div class="lesson-label">Higher-Level Lesson</div>

<h3>Opportunity is a system, not an event.</h3>

<p>
Many people search for opportunities by asking,
"What is available to me?"
A stronger question is:
"What sequence of actions would increase the number and quality
of opportunities available to me six months from now?"
</p>

<br>

<p>
That difference matters. A scholarship can reduce tuition.
A portfolio can create evidence. A mentor can create information
you cannot easily find online. A small project can produce a
case study. A temporary role can create industry experience.
The objective is therefore not simply to collect opportunities.
It is to create an <strong>opportunity pipeline</strong>.
</p>

</div>


